# ffmpeg sources fetched on demand by scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh.
# Each source tree is hundreds of MB; never commit.
sources/
build/

# Cargo build outputs for this crate's compile.
target/

# dist/ is a BUILD OUTPUT and is not committed.
#
# It once had to be. The archives are this crate's whole contract — build.rs
# panics rather than falling back on a system ffmpeg — and a cargo git
# checkout is not a place a build script can run, so a consumer resolving a
# git tag needed the archives already there.
#
# build.rs no longer works that way. `ensure_dist` builds into OUT_DIR (or
# $FFMPEG_BUNDLE_BUILD_DIR) at `dist-<identity>`, content-addressed by ffmpeg
# version, recipe and platform, and runs the recipe from source when that is
# absent — under a lock, so parallel cargo invocations compile it once. It
# never reads dist/ from the source tree.
#
# So committing dist/ now adds ~74MB of binaries per rebuild that nothing
# reads, and it can only ever hold ONE platform: a macOS dist/ carries
# libav*.a and `-framework VideoToolbox`, which is not what a Windows
# consumer links against. Per-platform is exactly what the content-addressed
# cache exists to do.
dist/
